{
  "_comment": [
    "Destinations the climate adapter rotates through for when-to-go posts.",
    "Chosen for where Israelis actually fly, not for coverage of the globe.",
    "`he` is the Hebrew name as it is normally written in Israel — the drafting",
    "step is told to use exactly this string rather than transliterating afresh",
    "each time, so the same city doesn't appear under two spellings across posts.",
    "",
    "`siteSlug` IS WHICH PAGE ON TIYULPLUS.COM THIS ROW IS, and it exists because",
    "the id usually is that and sometimes is not. A row with no siteSlug falls",
    "back to its id (see siteSlugFor in src/plan/site.js), which is right for the",
    "37 rows the site happens to name identically and wrong for the rest — and the",
    "cost of wrong is not an error, it is a post built from the AI route when a",
    "curated page was sitting there. Every value here was checked against a saved",
    "copy of /api/cities?options=1, which is in samples/site-cities.json, and a",
    "selftest holds them against it.",
    "",
    "SEVEN OF THEM POINT AT A PAGE WIDER THAN THE CITY: copenhagen, chiangmai,",
    "hanoi, dublin, osaka, sharm and malaga are entries on a regional page rather",
    "than pages of their own. They were not guessed. For each one, the distance",
    "from these coordinates to every place on the candidate page was measured, and",
    "the test each passed is that four or more of that page's places are within",
    "40km — Copenhagen's is 12 of 18. Candidates that failed it are left unmapped",
    "on purpose: naples→rome is 153km and istanbul→cappadocia is 528km, and a post",
    "closing on a page about somewhere else is a broken promise, not thin coverage."
  ],
